% Shorthand decorations followed by a chord symbol, an annotation or a
% decoration such as !p!, as in O "D" C (GitHub issue #84).  parsenote()
% (parseabc.c) required a note, a rest or a chord after the decorations,
% and reported a "Malformed note".  Tune 2 is the same music with the
% chord symbols and annotations first, as the abc standard orders them.
X:1
T:Decorations before chord symbols
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
H "C" C E G c |H"G" G B d g |T "^trill" c d e f |H !p! c2 H "C" [ce]2 |
H "Am" z A c e |]

X:2
T:Decorations after chord symbols
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
"C" H C E G c |"G"H G B d g |"^trill" T c d e f |!p! H c2 "C" H [ce]2 |
"Am" H z A c e |]
